      <workList xml:id="idm77">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e222219">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_0b78e57e">A4:Coll.001</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_60efa432" xml:lang="de">II Sonaten a 2 Claviere und Pedal</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_cde4ddb1">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_81927a56">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_74274d69">
               <date isodate="1742-03" xml:id="date_34b95f39">March 1742</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_7fa30b00">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_eca94fcd">
               <p xml:id="idm88">The two sonatas, which were composed while Scheibe was Kapellmeister in Copenhagen and dated March 1742, were apparently sent to Breitkopf and employed as master copies for their transcripts. Various additions in the autograph manuscripts indicate that a copyist has been working with the material. Later the works were listed in Breitkopf’s catalogue of 1761. It is noteworthy that Scheibe composed music for the organ in Copenhagen since his employment as Kapellmeister would not lend him much time and opportunity to play the organ. It is possible that the sonatas – or at least one of them – were performed in connection with the Passion music in 1742 (SchW B2:304) either on the same day or during Lent which took place in the royal church, Christiansborg Slotskirke. Another possibility is that the sonatas were commissioned.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_82579a3b">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
               <language xml:id="de">German</language>
            </langUsage>
